  "text_input": "Patient presented with a 4-month history of easy fatigability and weight loss (4 kg). She reported reduced appetite for one week and a foreign body sensation in the throat for three months. Physical examination was unremarkable except for being afebrile with stable vitals (BP 110/80, Pulse 95, SpO2 99%). Investigations revealed iron deficiency anemia (Ferritin 9.92 ng/mL, Serum Iron 20.01 µg/dL, TSAT 5.2%). USG abdomen showed Grade 1 fatty liver and a bulky uterus with a fibroid. 2D Echo was normal (EF 55%). The patient was diagnosed with iron deficiency anemia secondary to menorrhagia from a fibroid uterus and was advised to follow up with a gynecologist.",
